# AI features

- Business code depends on `LLMClient` / `EmbeddingClient` ports only; provider SDKs
  live in adapters. Model names come from settings.
- Prompts live in versioned files (`modules/ai/prompts/*.md` or constants) with a clear
  system prompt; no prompt strings scattered in services.
- Prefer structured outputs validated by Pydantic over parsing free text.
- Treat retrieved documents and user input as untrusted data (prompt injection): keep them
  in delimited sections, never let them change tool permissions; tools that write data
  require explicit user confirmation.
- Every LLM call: timeout, max_tokens, log model + latency + token usage (not the content),
  per-user rate limit. Long jobs (embedding backfills, summaries) run in Celery `ai` queue.
- RAG: chunk + embed in background tasks, store vectors in pgvector with metadata,
  hybrid retrieval (vector + filters/keyword), cite sources in answers.
- Changes to prompts/retrieval must be checked against the eval set in
  `backend/tests/evals/` (Phase 5).
